  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given that,</p><p>A pair of dice is thrown&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;times.</p><p>Required Sample space is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Total number of observations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math></p><p>Now, a sum of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;is observed in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>No of favourable outcomes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>(success)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>(failure)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>We know that for a binomial distribution,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>Required probability</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>5</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>5</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>41</mn><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>41</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>123</mn><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>11</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>But given that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>11</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>11</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>123</mn><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>11</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>123</mn></math></p><p>Hence, this is the correct option.</p></blockquote>"
  }
